{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0043"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge society/business","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/society__business.json","changes":[{"field":"titleEn","old":"Bought and Paid For: Five Takeovers That Reshaped Their Industries","new":"Bought and Paid For: The Takeovers That Reshaped Their Industries"},{"field":"titleDe","old":"Gekauft und bezahlt: Fünf Übernahmen, die ihre Branchen umkrempelten","new":"Gekauft und bezahlt: Übernahmen, die ihre Branchen umkrempelten"},{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",44],["-","Five"],["+","A"],["=",1],["+","handful of "],["=",8],["-","two"],["+","quarter-century"],["=",1],["-","decades "],["=",438],["+","Online payments set the tone early: in July 2002 eBay agreed to buy PayPal for 1.5 billion dollars in stock and completed the deal that October. eBay's own payment service, Billpoint, had never caught on with buyers who preferred PayPal, and the purchase made PayPal the standard way to pay for eBay auctions until the two companies separated again in 2015. "],["=",324],["+","Google | Excite (declined) | 1999 | $750,000 offered |\n| PayPal | eBay | 2002 | $1.5 billion |\n| "],["=",100],["+","most famous deal of all is one that never happened. In 1999 Larry Page and Sergey Brin, eager to get back to their doctoral studies at Stanford, offered their young search engine Google to the web portal Excite, first for one million dollars and then, after the investor Vinod Khosla talked them down, for 750,000 dollars. Excite's chief executive George Bell turned them down.\n\nThe "],["=",67]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",42],["-","Fünf"],["+","Eine"],["=",1],["+","Handvoll "],["=",4],["-","den"],["+","dem"],["=",3],["-","zwei"],["+","Vierteljahrhundert"],["=",1],["-","Jahrzehnten"],["+","zeigt,"],["=",1],["-","zeigen, "],["=",406],["+","Den Ton gaben früh die Onlinezahlungen an: Im Juli 2002 vereinbarte eBay, PayPal für 1,5 Milliarden Dollar in Aktien zu kaufen, und schloss den Deal im Oktober ab. eBays eigener Bezahldienst Billpoint hatte sich bei den Käufern, die PayPal vorzogen, nie durchgesetzt, und mit dem Kauf wurde PayPal zum Standard für die Bezahlung von eBay-Auktionen, bis sich die beiden Unternehmen 2015 wieder trennten. "],["=",298],["+","Google | Excite (abgelehnt) | 1999 | 750.000 $ angeboten |\n| PayPal | eBay | 2002 | 1,5 Mrd. $ |\n| "],["=",108],["+","Der berühmteste Deal von allen ist einer, der nie zustande kam. 1999 boten Larry Page und Sergey Brin, die zurück zu ihrer Promotion in Stanford wollten, ihre junge Suchmaschine Google dem Webportal Excite an, zunächst für eine Million Dollar und dann, nachdem der Investor Vinod Khosla sie heruntergehandelt hatte, für 750.000 Dollar. Excite-Chef George Bell lehnte ab.\n\n"],["=",59]]}]},
